      "polity": "Scythians (with Greek Black Sea colonies)",
      "summary": "Iranian-speaking Scythians ruled the steppe and forest-steppe from the Danube to the Don; Royal Scythians held the lower Dnieper. Herodotus (c. 440 BCE) described them in detail, and their kurgans (Solokha, Tovsta Mohyla) yielded famous gold work. Greek city-states founded colonies on the coast - Olbia, Tyras, Chersonesus, Panticapaeum - which formed the Bosporan Kingdom in the Kerch strait.",
