      "polity": "Left-bank Hetmanate (under the Tsardom of Russia)",
      "summary": "The Truce of Andrusovo (1667) partitioned Ukraine along the Dnieper: the Left Bank and Kyiv went to Muscovy, the Right Bank to Poland. Hetman Doroshenko's alliance with the Ottomans led to Ottoman rule over Podolia (1672-1699) and the devastation of the Right Bank. Hetman Ivan Mazepa (1687-1709) rebuilt the Left-bank Hetmanate, then sided with Charles XII of Sweden and was defeated at Poltava.",
