      "summary": "Ukrainian lands were administered as governorates of the Russian Empire ('Little Russia', 'New Russia') and as the Austrian crown land of Galicia and Lodomeria plus Bukovina; Transcarpathia belonged to Hungary. Ivan Kotliarevsky's Eneida (1798) began modern Ukrainian literature, Taras Shevchenko's Kobzar (1840) became its national symbol, and the 1848 Spring of Nations brought the first Ukrainian political body in Lviv.",
