      "endYear": 1932,
      "polity": "Ukrainian Soviet Socialist Republic",
      "summary": "The Ukrainian SSR was a founding republic of the USSR (30 December 1922), with its capital in Kharkiv. The 1920s policy of 'Ukrainization' (korenizatsiia) fostered Ukrainian culture, until Stalin's collectivization and purges ended it around 1929-1931. Western Ukrainian lands were ruled by Poland, Romania and Czechoslovakia.",
