      "summary": "Postwar treaties fixed Ukraine's western border: Transcarpathia was ceded by Czechoslovakia (1945) and the Polish-Soviet border followed roughly the Curzon line. The Ukrainian SSR became a founding member of the United Nations. Population exchanges with Poland, Operation Vistula (1947) and Soviet deportations reshaped the west, where the UPA fought on into the early 1950s; a further famine struck in 1946-1947.",
