      "startYear": 2004,
      "endYear": 2014,
      "polity": "Ukraine",
      "summary": "Mass protests against a rigged presidential run-off (the Orange Revolution) led to a re-vote won by Viktor Yushchenko. Viktor Yanukovych won in 2010; his last-minute refusal to sign the EU Association Agreement in November 2013 sparked the Euromaidan protests. After police and snipers killed about 100 protesters in February 2014, Yanukovych fled to Russia.",
